        s1: '1. Data',
        s1Text: (ip, mask) =>
          `<p>The IP address \\( ${ip} \\) and the subnet mask \\( ${mask} \\) are given in dotted decimal notation. Each of them is a sequence of \\( 32 \\) bits, split into four <b>octets</b>, that is groups of \\( 8 \\) bits: each number between the dots is the decimal value of one octet, from \\( 0 \\) to \\( 255 \\). To see which bits of the IP are selected by the mask, all the octets must be written in base \\( 2 \\).</p>`,

        s2: '2. Converting the octets from decimal to binary',
        s2Intro:
          `<p>Each octet is converted by successive division: the value is repeatedly divided by \\( 2 \\), writing down quotient and remainder, until the quotient becomes \\( 0 \\). The binary digits are the remainders read <b class="ipn-red-strong">from bottom to top</b>. An octet always has exactly \\( 8 \\) bits: if fewer than \\( 8 \\) digits are obtained, zeros are added on the left, which do not change the value.</p>`,
