        s3: '3. CIDR prefix: network bits and host bits',
        s3Text: (p) =>
          `<p>In the mask the \\( 1 \\)s are all consecutive starting from the left and are followed only by \\( 0 \\)s, so the mask is valid. The number of \\( 1 \\)s is the <b>CIDR prefix</b> (Classless Inter-Domain Routing: the slash notation, for example \\( /24 \\)). Here there are \\( ${p} \\) ones: the prefix is \\( /${p} \\).</p>`,
        s3Tex: (p, h) => `\\text{network bits} = ${p}, \\qquad \\text{host bits} = 32 - ${p} = ${h}`,
        boundary: (p) => {
          if (p === 0) return '<p>The mask contains no \\( 1 \\): no bit belongs to the network part.</p>';
